Audio fixtures for voice-stt integration tests live here. They're tracked
via git LFS (see ../../../../.gitattributes which globs *.wav / *.mp3 /
*.ogg / *.webm).

Required for tests/integration.test.ts:
  hello-world.wav  - any short clip whose transcription contains "hello"
                     or "world" (the assertion is lenient since whisper
                     transcription quality varies between models)

Generate with:
  ffmpeg -f lavfi -i 'sine=frequency=1000:duration=2' \
         -filter:a 'atempo=1.0' hello-world.wav

Or record locally:
  arecord -f S16_LE -r 16000 -c 1 -d 3 hello-world.wav
  # speak "hello world" during recording

Then:
  git add hello-world.wav   # LFS tracks it automatically
  git commit -m "test(voice-stt): add hello-world audio fixture"
